#emph[In plain terms:] only one of the ten findings is classified as a direct match to the declared target coordinates, and it comes from an immunosuppressed clinical allograft cohort \[48\] whose record, which rests on the abstract alone, lists the factors that predicted failure to reach insulin independence without an effect size for them. Six findings come from human stem-cell-derived cells assayed in culture and one from a graft in a mouse given a human immune system; each of those can support a bridged hypothesis about a human graft, never a transferred number. The two findings the classifier refuses are instructive. A large human genetic study of type 2 diabetes risk sits on a branch of the model-system axis that shares no common upper bound with a transplanted islet graft, so its odds ratio cannot be carried over. A result in an immortalized rat beta-cell line sits below the declared bridge floor, so it cannot be bridged either. A finding that cannot be carried over as support is still recorded, and both of these are cited as counter-evidence in §5.3.

#strong[What is and is not verified about these findings.] Every finding carries the verbatim sentence from which it was extracted. For this paper, all ten quoted sentences were located in the article text held by the National Center for Biotechnology Information: nine in PubMed Central full text, and one in a PubMed abstract, for the one study without a PubMed Central record (`t1d/check_t1d_vignette.py --quotes`). That check locates the quoted sentence only. It does not confirm the study arms, the direction, or the sample size, and it reads no PDF, so `primary_pdf_verified` is `false` on all ten findings and $I_5$ blocks every exact quantitative promotion in this bundle. The position of each finding on the four axes, which decides its transfer class, is the curator’s reading of the study design and not a field of the corpus. In particular, the forty recipients in `R1_0116:O1` received intraportal allografts under systemic immunosuppression \[48\]; assigning both that cohort and $c_(upright("target"))$ the coordinate `immunocompetent_auto_plus_allo_t1d` abstracts the presence of recipient autoimmune and allogeneic reactivity rather than absence of immunosuppression, whereas targeting an immunosuppression-free immune-evasive graft would leave treatment regimen as an unresolved bridge distinction. For the type 2 diabetes genetics study only the model-system coordinate carries meaning: a population cohort has no natural value on the other three axes, so those coordinates are placeholders, and its transfer class does not depend on them. The reading of the axes is the part of this example most open to disagreement, which is why the Discussion describes the context poset as a modeling commitment to be reviewed together with the graph.

=== 5.2 Curation replay from $D_0$ to $D_3$
<curation-replay-from-d_0-to-d_3>
The constructed starting bundle $D_0$ (SHA-256 prefix `5c38c177c0b7`) contains 8 studies, 20 arm variables and 10 evidence atoms. Three reversible `JSONPatch` events reach the settled corpus $D_3$ (SHA-256 prefix `fd1e9336453a`): `T1D-PATCH-001` retypes the $37 %$ decrease in type 2 diabetes risk in `R1_0340:O2` from `"point_level"` to `"relative_change"`, because a $37 %$ decrease is a relative change and not a measured level; `T1D-PATCH-002` restores the dropped second mutant arm `VAR:R1_0141:A8_iPSC_Lys34_hom` in the three-arm comparison `R1_0141:O9`\; and `T1D-PATCH-003` sets `requires_figure_digitization = true` on `R1_0215:O7`, which is read from a figure panel. Forward and inverse replay verify with zero errors, and all ten atoms satisfy $I_1$ binding against $D_3$.

These three defects are constructed for this example. $D_0$ was built by perturbing the settled records so that the replay has something to repair; the corrections are not errors found in the OpenIslet corpus, whose own 106-event curation ledger is replayed separately in §6.9. The settled values of all three, like the numbers, sample sizes and arm identifiers of Table 1, are the corpus values.

=== 5.3 Synthesis decisions and rejected probes
<synthesis-decisions-and-rejected-probes>
Five synthesis records verify against the settled bundle, with two terminal decisions between them. `T1D-CLIN-DIRECT-01` $arrow.r$ `QUALITATIVE_SCOPING_ONLY` records the one finding classified at the declared target coordinates, the immunosuppressed clinical cohort in which recipient #emph[SLC30A8] genotype, HLA-A\*24 positivity and body-mass index were independently associated with failure to reach insulin independence; because that record, which rests on the abstract alone, holds no effect size, it commits as a scoping note and asks for no number. The remaining four are cross-study hypotheses about a human islet graft, each built from evidence obtained outside that setting and each therefore `HOLD_FOR_PROSPECTIVE_FALSIFIER` behind a gate that names its unresolved axes, a head-to-head comparison, a read-out with units, and a numeric pass threshold.

- `T1D-CEG-H1-SLC30A8-INVERSION` $arrow.r$ `HOLD_FOR_PROSPECTIVE_FALSIFIER` (polarity `SCOPING_QUALIFICATION`) qualifies the protection against type 2 diabetes conferred by losing one copy of #emph[SLC30A8]. For an islet replacement setting, two records motivate caution without establishing that donor-cell #emph[SLC30A8] knockout causes graft loss: fewer #emph[INS]- and #emph[SLC30A8]-expressing cells form in vitro from stem-cell lines carrying premature-stop genotypes \[47\], and in the immunosuppressed clinical cohort \[48\] the recipient’s common #emph[SLC30A8] CT or TT genotype was independently associated with failure to achieve insulin independence (a recipient-genotype scoping signal on insulin independence rather than direct evidence about an engineered donor graft). Its gate (`GATE-H1-SLC30A8-MARGINAL-MASS`) asks for beta-like cell yield and twelve-week stimulated C-peptide from edited and unedited stem-cell-derived islets.
- `T1D-CEG-H2-NLRC5-UNCOUPLING` $arrow.r$ `HOLD_FOR_PROSPECTIVE_FALSIFIER` (polarity `CANDIDATE_UPGRADE`) proposes testing partial #emph[NLRC5] attenuation against #emph[STAT1] deletion: #emph[NLRC5] knockdown lowers interferon-induced HLA-ABC (`R1_0215:O7`), whereas #emph[STAT1] knockout reduces HLA class I and CXCL10 together with the inhibitory ligands HLA-E, PD-L1, and SOCS1 (`R1_0214:O12`, carried as counter-evidence). Because the same #emph[NLRC5] study \[50\] also observed reduced #emph[HLA-E] and 24-hour #emph[PD-L1] expression after #emph[NLRC5] knockdown in islet and beta-cell models (additional corpus outcomes outside this ten-finding subset), selective preservation of inhibitory ligands under partial attenuation is an unresolved empirical challenge rather than an established separation; its gate (`GATE-H2-NLRC5-VS-STAT1KO`) requires head-to-head suppression of HLA class I alongside retained HLA-E and PD-L1 surface expression and natural-killer-cell survival.
- `T1D-CEG-H4-CD55-ARMOR-PRESERVE-CD59` $arrow.r$ `HOLD_FOR_PROSPECTIVE_FALSIFIER` (polarity `CANDIDATE_UPGRADE`) proposes protecting cells with ectopic CD55, a complement regulator that is lower at the pancreatic endoderm stage than on endocrine cells, while leaving endogenous CD59 untouched, because knocking CD59 out strongly inhibits glucose-stimulated insulin secretion in a beta-cell line. Its gate (`GATE-H4-CD55-ECTOPIC-CD59-UNTOUCHED`) pairs survival in human serum complement with a dynamic perifusion secretion index.
- `T1D-CEG-H5-TXNIP-HYPOXIA-UNCOUPLING` $arrow.r$ `HOLD_FOR_PROSPECTIVE_FALSIFIER` (polarity `CANDIDATE_UPGRADE`) proposes editing the #emph[TXNIP] promoter in stem-cell-derived beta cells, which upregulate #emph[TXNIP] under the hypoxia a fresh graft meets, and reads the higher #emph[BCL2L1] expression of alpha-like cells as a sign that the two cell types differ in stress reserve. The #emph[BCL2L1] finding is a $0.13$ log2 fold difference measured under interferon-alpha and not under hypoxia, which is the kind of cross-condition step the gate exists to hold. Its gate (`GATE-H5-TXNIP-CIS-EDIT`) measures the ratio of insulin- to glucagon-positive cells fourteen days after a hypoxic episode.

#emph[In plain terms:] four cross-study hypotheses are written as candidate claims, and the gate holds all four. Each is a statement about a human islet graft built from evidence obtained outside that setting, so each must name the head-to-head experiment that would test it, with a read-out and a numeric pass threshold, before it can be written as anything stronger than a candidate. The fifth record is the one finding classified at the declared target coordinates; because its record holds no effect size, it commits as a scoping note and not as a number. Whether any of these four hypotheses is correct is not assessed here, and the experimental comparators and thresholds in their gates—for example whether `H4` also includes an unedited wild-type control alongside CD59-edited cells or whether `H5` pairs its cell-type ratio with absolute beta-cell survival and secretion—are proposals requiring domain review, because $I_4$ checks structural completeness of a falsifier gate rather than experimental-design sufficiency.

Four defective claims are submitted against the same bundle, and all four adversarial probes fail with their exact expected invariant codes. Promoting the type 2 diabetes odds ratio onto the islet-graft target is rejected as `I4_INADMISSIBLE_CONTEXT_TRANSFER`, and two further codes are raised alongside it. Writing an upgrade hypothesis without a prospective falsifier gate is rejected as `I4_MISSING_PROSPECTIVE_FALSIFIER_GATE`. Reading the odds ratio of $0.62$ as a $62 %$ decrease, when the source reports a $37 %$ decrease, is rejected as `I3_TOK_UNGROUNDED_VALUE`. Requesting a direct quantitative promotion from a finding whose source has not been certified is rejected as `I5_ILLEGAL_QUANTITATIVE_PROMOTION_WITHOUT_PRIMARY_OR_DIGITIZED_SOURCE`.

#emph[In plain terms:] the third probe catches a subtle numeric misreading. The primary genetics study \[46\] reports both a $37 %$ decrease in type 2 diabetes risk and an additive-model odds ratio of $0.62$—two distinct, non-equivalent summary measures, because an odds ratio is not a risk ratio and $1 - 0.62 = 0.38 eq.not 0.37$ (the vignette atom records the $37 %$ `relative_change` quantity alongside the corpus entry’s `odds_ratio` statistic tag). Reading the $0.62$ odds ratio as a $62 %$ decrease invents an unsupported percentage in a sentence that still cites the right study.

